    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. can you dig a bit deeper into the fee structures? sometimes there are hidden costs or things that pop up in mutual funds that make them more expensive over time compared to etfs. what should i look out for regarding those extra expenses?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In mutual funds, watch out for high **Expense Ratios** and **Sales Loads** (front-end or back-end fees paid to the seller). ETFs typically have much lower expense ratios because many are passively managed, leading to lower long-term costs. Be wary in mutual funds of \"12b-1 fees,\" which are embedded marketing and distribution charges not always obvious in the basic expense ratio. Generally, the lower operating costs of ETFs translate into more direct, predictable investing for the client.",
      "source": "target",
